---
id: soy-ginger-sesame-shrimp
title: Soy-Ginger-Sesame Shrimp (Poke Style)
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 3
  cooked_g: 600

storage:
  fridge_days: 2
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Thaw: tip both bags of @cooked-pacific-white-shrimp{2%package} into a large bowl of cold tap water with 2 tsp of salt. Let sit for ~thaw-time{10%min} (7 to 10 minutes) until completely thawed, then pinch the tails off.

Dry: spread the shrimp on 4 to 5 sheets of paper towel and press dry. Wet shrimp dilute the marinade and it won't stick.

Mix: in a large bowl, stir together 3 tbsp of @soy-sauce-less-sodium{3%tbsp}, 2 tsp of @sesame-oil{2%tsp}, 2 tsp of @rice-vinegar{2%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/2%tsp}, and @ground-ginger{1/2%tsp}. Add the dried shrimp and stir to coat.

Rest: let sit for ~rest-time{5%min} at room temperature, stirring once.

Divide the shrimp and marinade equally into 3 meal prep containers (about 200 g per portion). To serve, spoon over a warm base (rice or buckwheat) and pour the liquid from the container over the top.
